WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.880
Quantum threats matter because security planning has to begin before a crisis is visible.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.420
The practical concern is not that every current system is already broken.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.440
The concern is that large cryptographically relevant quantum computers could weaken widely

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.860
used public-key cryptography,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.110
and the systems that depend on that cryptography often take years to discover, change,

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.000
test, approve, and deploy.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.525
Security practitioners need to distinguish present-day risk, future capability,

00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:25.120
and migration lead time.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.670
Present-day risk includes data being collected now, systems being designed now,

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.580
and products being purchased now.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.305
Future capability refers to the possibility that quantum computers eventually become

00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:37.630
strong enough to attack certain public-key schemes.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.230
Migration lead time is the gap between deciding to change and actually changing complex

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.680
systems safely.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.190
Public-key cryptography is the central concern because it supports key exchange,

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.200
digital signatures, certificates, identity, software trust, and many secure protocols.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.575
Symmetric cryptography and hashing are affected differently,

00:00:53.575 --> 00:00:55.000
and the response is not the same.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.670
The migration problem is therefore not simply replace encryption everywhere.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.610
It is identify where specific public-key functions create future exposure.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.800
Planning matters most for systems with long lifetimes, long data sensitivity periods,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.840
and complex dependencies.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.240
A web service that can be updated monthly is different from a medical device, satellite,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.880
vehicle, industrial controller, or long-lived archive.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.920
The goal of quantum readiness is not fear.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.025
It is disciplined preparation while there is still time to inventory, prioritize, test,

00:01:21.025 --> 00:01:21.560
and coordinate.
